<!-- DROP-IN SEQUENCE: THE AMBUSH & THE PURSUIT              -->
<!-- ======================================================= -->

<div class="slugline">EXT. PRAGUE-LIBEŇ - JUNCTION OF KIRCHMAYEROVA AND V HOLEŠOVIČKÁCH - DAY (MAY 27, 1942 - 10:35 AM)</div>

<p class="action">
Dazzling midday glare. A sharp, downhill cobblestone curve where Kirchmayerova Avenue sweeps into V Holešovičkách. Overhead, electrical tram wires crisscross the sky.
</p>

<p class="action">
The dark-green open Mercedes-Benz 320 (SS-3) brakes hard to navigate the steep hairpin turn. 
</p>

<p class="action">
Standing on the pavement curb: JOZEF GABČÍK (30). He drops his raincoat to the dirt, stepping straight into the roadway directly in front of the decelerating radiator grille.
</p>

<p class="action">
In his hands: a British STEN MK II SUBMACHINE GUN. Gabčík braces the skeleton stock against his hip, takes aim point-blank at Heydrich's chest, and squeezes the trigger.
</p>

<p class="action">
A dry, hollow, metallic SNAP. The 9mm cartridge misfeeds. The bolt JAMS.
</p>

<p class="action">
In the front seat, driver SS-Oberscharführer JOHANNES KLEIN reaches for the floor shift to accelerate—standard escape protocol.
</p>

<p class="action">
Heydrich slaps Klein’s arm away with a violent backhand.
</p>

<div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
<div class="parenthetical">(screaming over the engine)</div>
<div class="dialogue">Halt! Sofort anhalten!</div>

<p class="action">
Klein stamps the floorboard brake. Tires SCREECH across the rails. 
</p>

<p class="action">
Instead of ducking, Heydrich leaps to his feet inside the open car. He unholsters his WALTHER PPK (7.65mm) and chambers a round, barking with furious, arrogant disdain.
</p>

<p class="action">
Behind the car, JAN KUBIŠ lunges from behind a streetlamp. He swings an arm like a bowler, hurling a MODIFIED NO. 73 ANTI-TANK GRENADE.
</p>

<p class="action">
The bomb does not land inside. It strikes the right rear wheel well.
</p>

<p class="action">
A CATACLYSMIC ROAR.
</p>

<p class="action">
The blast punches the rear of the Mercedes off its suspension. The right side-panel disintegrates into flying metal, wheel splinters, pulverized seat padding, and coarse upholstery horsehair. Shrapnel cuts Kubiš across the brow; blood blinds his left eye as he staggers backward.
</p>

<p class="action">
Acrid, gray-black smoke engulfs the junction. Passing tram No. 3 jerks to a screeching halt. Passengers hit the floorboards inside the cars.
</p>

<p class="action">
Inside the smoke, there is no heroic pause. Only frantic, ugly desperation.
</p>

<p class="action">
Gabčík tosses the dead Sten into the gutter, spins on his heel, and sprints up the Kirchmayerova hill toward the tram island.
</p>

<p class="action">
Through the swirling cordite smoke, the passenger door violently KICKS open.
</p>

<p class="action">
HEYDRICH EMERGES ON HIS FEET.
</p>

<p class="action">
His uniform is shredded at the lower flank; his tunic is blackened by blast soot. Flooded with massive combat adrenaline, he feels no pain yet—only animal rage.
</p>

<p class="action">
With his Walther PPK extended in his right hand, Heydrich SPRINTS into the intersection, pursuing Gabčík uphill.
</p>

<p class="action">
CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!
</p>

<p class="action">
Heydrich fires three wild rounds at Gabčík’s retreating back. Pedestrians scream and scatter behind lampposts. 
</p>

<p class="action">
Gabčík pulls a COLT M1903 POCKET HAMMERLESS from his pocket, spinning mid-stride to snap two return shots. The bullets ricochet off the cobblestones near Heydrich’s boots.
</p>

<p class="action">
Heydrich raises his Walther to fire a fourth round—CLICK. The pistol jams, or the magazine is spent.
</p>

<p class="action">
Fifteen paces up the hill, the adrenaline shock cliff drops out from underneath him.
</p>

<p class="action">
Heydrich STUMBLES. His face drains instantly from furious red to a hideous, wet, chalky grey. A deep, guttural groan rips from his throat.
</p>

<p class="action">
His left hand clamps over his lower left flank. Dark, venous blood wells between his long fingers. Internally, his 11th rib is shattered, his diaphragm torn, his spleen pulverized.
</p>

<p class="action">
He cannot draw breath. His legs turn to water. 
</p>

<p class="action">
Heydrich staggers backward down the incline, clutching lampposts and tram poles to stay upright, dragging his boots until he reaches the shattered Mercedes.
</p>

<p class="action">
He collapses chest-first over the warm steel of the hood, choking on his own blood.
</p>

<p class="action">
Driver Klein runs around the vehicle, service pistol drawn, panicked.
</p>

<div class="character">KLEIN</div>
<div class="dialogue">Herr Obergruppenführer!</div>

<div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
<div class="parenthetical">(coughing, spray of blood hitting the radiator)</div>
<div class="dialogue">Fassen Sie den Hund! Den Kerl... get him!</div>

<p class="action">
Klein turns and sprints up Kirchmayerova, chasing Gabčík into Brauner’s butcher shop (řeznictví)—where Gabčík will shoot Klein twice in the thigh and escape into the alleys.
</p>

<p class="action">
Left completely alone in the smoke, Heydrich slides off the hood onto the filthy cobblestones. 
</p>

<p class="action">
His fingers claw weakly at his waistband. The architect of the Police State lies bleeding in the gutter of an occupied capital, waiting for a passing delivery truck to haul him to Bulovka Hospital.
</p>

